body.stem:
Two lock levels are exposed in the Azure portal: 'Delete' and 'Read-only'. Your team must recreate those same lock levels by using Azure PowerShell. The portal labels and the behavior associated with each are shown in the following code block.

```
{
  "Azure portal lock names and behaviors": [
    { "name": "Delete",     "behavior": "Authorized users can read and modify the resource, but cannot delete it." },
    { "name": "Read-only",  "behavior": "Authorized users can read the resource, but cannot delete or modify it." }
  ]
}
```

What values should you assign to the LockLevel parameter of the New-AzResourceLock cmdlet?

